<title>UK: ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in December.</title>
<headline>ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in December.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The buffer stock manager of the International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) announced on Thursday the buffer stock sales planned for December would total 4,250 tonnes and would comprise the following cocoa, an ICCO press release said.</p>
<p>The date of the sale has yet to be announced.</p>
<p>Details of the cocoa offered for sale are as follows.</p>
<p>ORIGIN	  TONNES	PORT	CROP	  QUALITY</p>
<p>Cameroon	  179     Amsterdam   1982/83	GF</p>
<p>Cameroon	  100     Amsterdam   1982/83	FF</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire    10     Amsterdam   1979/80	FF</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   322     Amsterdam   1981/82	GF</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   150     Amsterdam   1981/82	FF</p>
<p>Ghana	     254     Amsterdam   1986/87	GF</p>
<p>Ghana	     397     Hull	  1981/82	GF</p>
<p>Ghana	   1,290     Hull	  1987/88	GF</p>
<p>Ghana	     298     Hull	  1987/88	FF</p>
<p>Nigeria	    99     Amsterdam   1980/81	GF</p>
<p>Nigeria	   139     Amsterdam   1980/81	FF</p>
<p>Nigeria	   249     Amsterdam   1986/87	GF</p>
<p>Nigeria	   249     Amsterdam   1986/87	FF</p>
<p>The following parcels to be sold as per sample drawn and approved by buyers.</p>
<p>								     WAREHOUSE</p>
<p>								     KEEPER</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   99  Amsterdam   1981/82    FAQ     Nedveem</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   49  Amsterdam   1981/82    FAQ Ocean Warehousing</p>
<p>							     (H.D. Cotterell)</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   51  Amsterdam   1987/88    FAQ Handelsveem b.v.</p>
<p>Nigeria	  196  Amsterdam   1980/81    FAQ     Nedveem b.v.</p>
<p>Nigeria	  119  Amsterdam   1980/81    FAQ Ocean Warehousing</p>
<p>							     (H.D. Cotterell)</p>
<p>GF: good fermented, FF: fair fermented, FAQ: fair to average quality</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newroom +44-171-542 8072</p>
